--- run_self_test help ---
usage: miniwdl run_self_test [-h] [--dir DIR] [--cfg FILE] [--as-me] [--no-quant-check] [-p DIR]
                             [--debug]

optional arguments:
  -h, --help          show this help message and exit
  --dir DIR           run the test in specified directory, instead of some new temporary directory
  --cfg FILE          configuration file to load (in preference to file named by MINIWDL_CFG
                      environment, or XDG_CONFIG_{HOME,DIRS}/miniwdl.cfg)
  --as-me             run all containers as the current user uid:gid
  --debug             maximally verbose logging & exception tracebacks

language:
  --no-quant-check    relax static typechecking of optional types, and permit coercion of T to
                      Array[T] (discouraged; for backwards compatibility with older WDL)
  -p DIR, --path DIR  local directory to search for imports
--- run self test ---
